        "statement_id": "factory_rejects_above_100000",
        "role": "root_cause",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "evidence_id": "e_244b113541c8_0003",
            "text": "The dynamic fee system contains a cconflicting fee caps between `DynamicSwapFeeModule.getFee()` and `CLFactory.getSwapFee()` which renders the dynamic fee mechanism ineffective. The `DynamicSwapFeeModule` allows fees up to 500,000 (50%) internally, but `CLFactory.getSwapFee()` rejects any fee above 100,000 (10%), causing the system to always fall back to basic tick spacing fees."
          },
          {
            "evidence_id": "e_244b113541c8_0005",
            "text": "And in CLFactory the getSwapFee function rejects any fee above 100,000 (10%), upon which it falls back to the default tick spacing fee."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "statement_id": "dynamic_fee_above_10pct_rejected",
        "role": "action",
        "evidence": [
          {
            "evidence_id": "e_244b113541c8_0006",
            "text": "As a result, any dynamically calculated fee above 10% gets rejected reducing potential protocol revenue. Potential user discounts applied in `getFee()` are lost when the factory rejects the final fee. And the 50% anti-MEV protection cap becomes unusable, leaving pools vulnerable to maximal extractable value attacks during high volatility"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
